# XCU get
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# SCCS files are made and inspected only with the SCCS utilities (admin,
# get, delta, prs and friends); the file format is unspecified so nothing
# reads the files directly. A missing companion utility makes the test
# UNRESOLVED. Login names, dates and the diagnostic texts are never compared
# literally.

assertion  XCU.get.001
anchor     utilities/get.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/get.html#STDERR
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -p writes the text to standard output and moves the informative
           lines to standard error, and -s with -p drops them.
test       t/001-print-option.sh

assertion  XCU.get.002
anchor     utilities/get.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/get.html#OUTPUT FILES
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       get writes the SID and line count to standard output and creates
           a read-only g-file with the retrieved text.
test       t/002-g-file.sh

assertion  XCU.get.003
anchor     utilities/get.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/get.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/get.html#OUTPUT FILES
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -e reports the new delta SID, creates a writable g-file and a
           p-file, and blocks a second get -e on the same SID.
test       t/003-edit.sh

assertion  XCU.get.004
anchor     utilities/get.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -r picks a version, -t takes the top delta of a release or level,
           and a late cutoff with -c keeps every delta.
test       t/004-select-version.sh

assertion  XCU.get.005
anchor     utilities/get.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/get.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       Keywords %M% %I% %Z% %W% %F% are replaced in the retrieved text
           and -k leaves them alone.
test       t/005-keywords.sh

assertion  XCU.get.006
anchor     utilities/get.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -m prefixes each line with its SID and a tab, -n with the module
           name and a tab, and both give the module name, SID and text.
test       t/006-prefix-m-n.sh

assertion  XCU.get.007
anchor     utilities/get.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/get.html#OUTPUT FILES
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -g retrieves no text but succeeds only for an existing SID, and
           -l writes an l-file listing the applied delta.
test       t/007-no-text-and-l-file.sh

assertion  XCU.get.008
anchor     utilities/get.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -x leaves a delta out of the generated text.
test       t/008-exclude.sh

assertion  XCU.get.009
anchor     utilities/get.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       With no -r the latest delta is read and its successor made, -r
           with a higher release makes release.1, and -r of an earlier delta
           that has a successor makes a branch SID.
test       t/009-sid-table.sh

assertion  XCU.get.010
anchor     utilities/get.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/get.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/get.html#STDIN
class      required
since      1992
says       With several SCCS files, a directory or "-" as the operand, get
           processes every named SCCS file (for "-" the names are read from
           standard input), writes each pathname followed by a colon on a
           line of its own before the informative lines, and silently
           ignores non-SCCS files in a directory.
test       t/010-multiple-operands.sh

assertion  XCU.get.011
anchor     utilities/get.html#OPTIONS/-L
class      required
since      1992
says       With -L the delta summary is written to standard output, the
           informative lines go to standard error, and -s suppresses them.
test       t/011-L-summary.sh

assertion  XCU.get.012
anchor     utilities/get.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       Using -x lists the excluded deltas after a line "Excluded:", and
           using -i lists the included deltas after a line "Included:", on
           standard output.
test       t/012-included-excluded.sh

assertion  XCU.get.013
anchor     utilities/get.html#OPTIONS/-b
class      required
since      1992
says       With -e, -b makes the new delta a branch when the b flag is set
           and the retrieved delta is a leaf, and is ignored when the flag
           is absent or the retrieved delta is not a leaf.
test       t/013-branch-b.sh
